error Failure { Failed; }

// Unary `!` in an `if` condition (card `BITWISE-CONDITIONS`), lowered onto
// `source.branch.v1` (card `IF-STATEMENT`) by an **arm swap**.
//
// `if (!C) { A } else { B }` is exactly the branch a reader would have written
// as `if (C) { B } else { A }`, and this fixture's emitted C is byte-identical
// to that twin's. The negation is therefore a pure token-tier construct: no
// operation, no checker rule, no core IR node, and nothing downstream can tell
// a `!` was written.
//
// The two arms are deliberately **distinguishable** — one carries a
// `qcore_check` the other does not — so the byte equality is a statement about
// the swap rather than about two identical arms. They are nonetheless
// custody-equal, because a check leaves the ledger alone, which is what the
// join requires.
//
fn main() -> i32 {
    let a = qcore_acquire(1, true, Failure);
    if (!(3 < 5)) {
        qcore_check(true, Failure);
        drop a;
    } else {
        drop a;
    }
    return 0;
}
